hey everybody how's it going my name is  mayuko and welcome back to my channel  you'll notice this beautiful new  addition to my desk  yes it's so pretty i'm so excited to  talk about it today i'm going to be  talking to you about my new monitor and  yes as the title suggests it's something  that i didn't think that i would want or  need but now that i'm using it i'm like  dang  i've been missing out this is this is a  good freaking monitor so yes we're gonna  be talking about my monitor today i've  talked about my desk setup in numerous  different points throughout the year  because it just keeps evolving  including things like my keyboard my  desk met and now this gorgeous new thing  thank you so much to lg for working with  me on this video they gifted me this  lovely monitor and i've used it for  about a week and so today we're gonna  dive in and tell you what i like and  don't like about it okay so first let's  start off with the specs so that you all  know what we're working with here this  is the 34 inch 21x9 ultra wide qhd ips  display from lg it's got an ergonomic  stand which is one of the main features  of this monitor specifically so yes this  is my very first ultra wide monitor and  that's one of the first things i want to  talk about how has it been when you go  using an ultra wide monitor because  wasn't your thing like using a 27 inch  monitor which yes using a 27-inch  monitor was indeed my thing like that's  the thing i've been using for like six  years been through many different brands  but like 27 inch was like a perfect size  for me and so even before setting this  one up i just had one single 27 inch  monitor that was using i use this  monitor setup for writing and editing  and coding and checking emails and  watching youtube but also running xcode  and running premiere pro so like i do  everything from the gamut of just like  some light internet browsing to heavy  pinteresting to some really kind of like  resource intensive very space  intensive stuff that requires a lot of  multitasking a lot of windows open kind  of thing but yeah the tldr basically is  that i love this thing wow how have i  not used ultra wide form factors up  until this point because oh baby have i  been missing out because let me tell you  i think for a long time i was kind of  this like the more monitors the better  the more monitors you have the more  badass you look at work the more  monitors you have the more productive  that you're probably gonna be and uh and  then i realized about like six months  ago that that wasn't the case and i was  just like okay let's let's do some  digital minimalism let's just go with  one monitor because you can't like focus  on more than one app at a time so why  have multiple monitors open so i was  pretty happy with that i did a lot of  multitasking on that one 27-inch monitor  i will say it got me more focused  because i couldn't have multiple apps  open at the same time but sometimes it  just didn't feel like enough space i  will say but i was like willing to live  with it sort of  and then lg sent me this monitor and i  was like you know what doesn't hurt to  try let's just see what the fuss is all  about and uh yeah  it's great i like it specifically  because it's still one monitor there you  don't have like a split in the middle  because of two monitors and so you can  have apps across all the different parts  of the screen and yes it like most of  the time i have more than one app open  in one kind of screen but it does allow  me to have multiple apps open at the  same time which a lot of my work  requires the use of more than one app  because i'm like looking at my notes  from notion and writing them to another  page on notion or i'm looking at one  page on notion and then i'm like putting  it into premiere pro or i'm looking at  something on brave and then taking notes  in notion i use notion a lot and so it's  really nice to just have like just so  much space to have that it's like having  three three windows open on a monitor is  the equivalent of having two  uh windows open on a 27 inch so yeah  there's a lot of space for stuff which  is really nice so yes form factor wise i  will rate this monitor a 10 out of 10  stars misubi's  wonderful little smiley faces i don't  know it's i  i like it i really like it i also like  that it's not too wide um i think the  thing that prevented me from using an  ultra web monitor to begin with was i  didn't like how curved it can be because  i don't like the feeling of being  swallowed by my technology and swallowed  by my screen but this one has a really  nice gentle curve to it that allows you  to see all four corners of the screen  really clearly but uh it's it's like it  still doesn't feel like i'm just being  swallowed whole you know the next thing  that i want to talk about with regards  to this monitor and what i like about it  is the swivel stand i learned about this  monitor because i watched a video from  jossie who reviewed this very monitor  and i was like that stand looks really  clean and really useful and so that's  one of the reasons why i was really  interested in testing this out basically  this stand allows you to move your  monitor in every direction which is so  nice doesn't even come with like a  monitor like a traditional monitor stand  it comes with this like desk mount thing  like most other monitors you have to buy  this separately i used to have like a  monitor  stand that i would attach two of my  monitors to onto my desk but this one  just comes with it and wow it's really  easy to move things flexibly it feels  like it's just gonna  work and i feel like it's not very like  wobbly or shaky or janky or anything  like that and i will say most of the  time yes my monitor is in this position  so there's not a whole lot of swivelly  action but modest is a standing desk  also i like moving my desk to different  parts of my room to work and stuff and  so when that happens like making sure  that i can change my monitor position  really easily no matter where i'm at or  how i want to use my desk just makes it  super easy like i don't have to climb  behind my desk and like unscrew stuff  and loosen screws and tighten screws i  used to have to do that and it was a  pain in the butt there's actually one  very specific use case that i like using  the swivel stand sometimes i set up my  camera right there or like i want to set  it up right here but the monitor is in  the way so literally i'll just move it  and then it's not in the way and i can  still see my monitor for notes and i can  still look at the camera and the camera  it doesn't have the monitor in view so  yes the ergostand offers an expanded  ergonomic adjustment of extend retract  swivel height and tilt as well as  providing a perfect position of the  screen for a more comfortable and  sustainable user experience  because yes ergonomics is important when  you sit at your desk for so long every  single day like i feel it in my  shoulders if it's not the right position  and so having my tools kind of like move  and shift around me so that i  don't like  hurt  pretty important stuff so the next  feature that i want to talk about that i  really like about this monitor is this  whole kind of like plug-in capability i  don't actually know if like this is  super unique to this one but i will say  this is something that i like about this  one basically it has usb ports on the  back and so as long as you connect your  computer to this monitor using the usbc  port you'll be able to connect  peripherals to the monitor which then  will be able to connect to the computer  through that usbc cable which is game  changing because the freaking macbook  pro only has like four ports so it's  kind of important there's like most of  the time when i have like an external  monitor and periphery devices i use all  four ports but literally with this setup  i only have to plug in one  so i have my webcam  and my speakers and my keyboard plugged  into the monitor and then because the  monitor is also charging literally i  just plug in that usbc into my macbook  and i can use all of those things and it  charges i can't tell you how excited i  was when i figured out that's like how  it worked because i was just like  i don't have to use dongles on goggles  on dongles like  oh that's so nice  especially because i i don't know i just  like having a minimal setup and i don't  want cords everywhere so the core  management was also just super easy for  this oh and speaking of cord management  that's another plus of this monitor it's  got really excellent gourd management i  gotta say so all the cords that come out  from the back of the monitor you can  actually kind of like guide it down the  whole ergonomic stand which comes with  like a cover so you can really just hide  away all of your cords and so i don't  have to see any of the cords that are  plugged into my monitor even though i  have a bunch and yeah you know most  monitors come with some sort of cord  management these days but i was just  really happy that this was like super  built in and i didn't have to use like  super dinky looking like cord management  ties and stuff and like invent my own  solution like no it was built in as part  of the monitor so yes this monitor has a  lot going for it it's got really great  swivel stand the form factor is great  the cord management is great the only  con that i can think of for this monitor  which to me is not really that big of a  deal breaker is that the color looks a  little faded compared to even something  like the macbook pro screen it just  looks like the colors a bit white or  like like white washed kind of faded  sort of looking i try to mess with the  different uh settings on it and stuff  but it doesn't really help and so  compared to other monitors out there out  of the box uh with some basic settings  and stuff without doing anything super  fancy  the color is fine which for me like i'm  either coding or writing or if i am  color grading like that kind of makes a  difference uh but not so much that i'm  just like  i don't have a sense of what my color  image is supposed to look like at all  like it's fine but i i think it could be  a little bit better so if you're someone  who needs like super vivid colors and  stuff you know maybe assess that about  this monitor but i i mean for like  everyday use where you're not doing like  really intense color grading stuff where  you need the colors to be super true and  super vivid  not a huge deal so all in all this  monitor really surprised me i really  like it and  uh for the price i think it's something  that i would buy if a company was gonna  buy it for me like if i worked at a  company and then they were like what do  you want for your desk setup i would  definitely choose this one would i pay  that money myself  i'm not really sure i'm just not someone  who wants to invest that much like money  into my desk setup honestly but if you  are someone who wants to i think this is  well worth it so yeah i'm just generally  very surprised by how much i like this  thing using it for the last week i'm  kind of just like how did i ever not use  this like i can't believe i wrote off  ultra wide monitors to begin with  so  yeah just it's it's the whole package  everything is great about it really  there's that only one issue that i would  change and you know that's not such a  big deal for me so i would absolutely  absolutely recommend this monitor thank  you so much to lg for partnering with me  on this video and sending me this  monitor if you'd like to find out more  about the monitor then i'll leave a link  in the description box down below so  yeah hope you like my review of this  monitor let me know what you think in  the comments down below also if you own  this monitor let me know what you think  about it don't forget to subscribe to my  channel for more you know setup review  kind of stuff like this as well as other  tech career in life videos hope y'all  are having a great day and i'll see you  next time bye

